# Revisions git blame should skip — bulk reformats with no behaviour change.
#
# Without this, `git blame` on any line touched by a formatting sweep names the sweep instead of
# the person and reason behind the code. That matters here: debugging in this estate leans hard on
# "when did this change, and why?", and a blame that answers "style: adopt prettier" has destroyed
# exactly the information you needed.
#
# Locally, enable it once per clone:
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
# GitHub honours this file automatically in its blame view.
#
# Only ever add commits that are PROVABLY behaviour-free (typecheck + full suite green on both
# sides). A functional change hidden in here would be invisible to blame forever.

# style: adopt prettier (printWidth 110, singleQuote) — 226 files, 1080 tests green either side
